hadiths[count]{hadithnumber,text}:
"1660","**\nNarrated to us Muhammad ibn Rafi’, narrated to us Suraij ibn al-Nu’man, who said: Narrated to us Fulaikh, from Sa’eed ibn al-Harith, from Abu Salamah ibn ‘Abd al-Rahman, who said: When Abu Hurayrah passed away, I said, \"By Allah, I should go to Abu Sa’eed al-Khudri.\" So I went to him and he narrated a lengthy hadith about the story of the palm branches.\n\nThen the sky became stormy that night. When the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) went out for the ‘Isha prayer, a flash of lightning illuminated the sky. He (ﷺ) saw Qatadah ibn al-Nu’man and said, \"Why are you here at this hour, O Qatadah?\"\n\nQatadah replied, \"I knew, O Messenger of Allah, that few people would attend the prayer tonight, so I wanted to attend it.\"\n\nThe Prophet (ﷺ) said, \"If you have prayed, then remain in your place until I pass by you.\"\n\nWhen he (ﷺ) finished the prayer, he (ﷺ) gave Qatadah a palm branch and said, \"Take this. It will illuminate for you ten steps ahead and ten steps behind you. When you enter your house and see darkness in a corner of the house, strike it before you speak, for it is the Shaytan.\"\n\nQatadah did so, and we love these palm branches for that reason."
